@startuml SmallAIOS Incident Response Workflow
' Incident Response Workflow per NIST SP 800-61
' SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

skinparam backgroundColor white

title Incident Response Workflow (NIST SP 800-61)

|Automated|
start
:Event detected;
note right
  Sources:
  - Monitoring thresholds
  - Audit log anomaly
  - Watchdog timeout
  - External report
end note

:Classify severity;
if (Severity?) then (Critical/High)
  :Publish incident event\n(smallaios/v1/incidents);
  :Execute automated containment;
  note right
    - Capability revocation
    - Task termination
    - Connection reset
    - Inference rejection
  end note
  :Preserve evidence;
  note right
    - Export audit log batches
    - Capture task snapshots
    - Export memory stats
    - Export capability registry
  end note
else (Medium/Low)
  :Log incident event;
  :Adjust monitoring thresholds;
endif

|Human|
:Incident Commander notified;
if (Severity?) then (Critical)
  :Activate full response team;
  :Isolate affected system;
  :Invoke emergency CCB;
else (High)
  :Security Lead + CCB member;
  :Increase monitoring;
else (Medium)
  :Security Lead review;
  :Schedule CCB discussion;
else (Low)
  :Security Lead tracks;
  :Continue normal ops;
endif

:Analyze root cause;
:Determine eradication actions;
:Apply corrective patch;
note right
  Emergency: Security Lead + 1 CCB
  Normal: Standard CCB process
end note

:Verify fix via test suite;
:Restore from known-good baseline;
:Resume operations with\nincreased monitoring (24-48h);

|Post-Incident|
:Conduct post-incident review\n(within 5 business days);
:Write post-incident report;
:Enter corrective actions\nin POA&M;
:Present to steering committee;
:Update incident response plan\n(lessons learned);

stop

@enduml
